For "not applicable": no memory to stand on; fine; if the task needs project knowledge, that's 3.1's "missing" → research/preparation piece, not memory-check's failure.

This gives a coherent principle: **memory-check at 3.1 tells the design what memory it may rely on. It does not decide whether the task runs; it decides what the run may stand on.** That's the one-line thesis. Great.

